{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/8092-dtf-looking-for-ideas-to-put-a-gnostic-spin-to-the-setting","id":8092,"title":"[DtF] Looking for ideas to put a gnostic spin to the setting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-11T08:06:36-08:00","id":8092,"title":"[DtF] Looking for ideas to put a gnostic spin to the setting","content":"After a weird (although deep) philosophical chat with an old friend, I'm looking for input to alter the original Demon setting to either include or conform to Gnostic beliefs. My idea is to keep the background roughly similar, with a gnostic interpretation of the Creator and the Host.<br /> <br /> Although I'm far from being an expert in the field, I'm toying with the following ideas:<ul><li>The Creator is the Demiurge, and the Angels Its Archons. At first, no one but the Demiurge knew of a higher reality, and the Archons built the fallen world at the Demiurge's command.</li> <li>Lucifer and a third of the Host achieved Gnosis and, in doing so, pierced the illusion of the Demiurge and sought to uplift mankind and leave the corrupt physical world behind.</li> <li>The Fall was a last-ditch effort of the Demiurge to prevent this from happening, severing the fallen world from the Emanations of the True God altogether, leaving behind a world of darkness.</li> <li>After the cataclysm, the Demiurge parted from the fallen world along with its Archons and set out to create another one from scratch.</li> <li>The Abyss is the gulf of nothingness caused by the Demiurge, where the rebel Archons were trapped by the Demiurge during the Fall.</li> </ul>So... any ideas, suggestions, criticism, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":355,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/355-romanov","user":"romanov","date":".  DtF, Demon, Gnosticism 11-11-2013, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/355-romanov","name":"romanov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T07:04:11-08:00","id":9653,"title":"","content":"Color me impressed. Demon: The Fallen is originally based on Paradise Lost, which is originally based on medieval Christian teaching about Lucifer falling from heaven, which is originally based on a misinterpretation and mistranslation of a couple passages in the New Testament. In short, the game is the end result of a game of telephone... but you've managed to make it map onto one branch of Gnosticism pretty well with a minimum effort.<br /> <br /> How does this impact the setting? How are things different because of it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1021-raneth","name":"Raneth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T09:39:39-08:00","id":9773,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Raneth. I borrowed some ideas from Mage: the Awakening, where the Abyss is what keeps the Realms Supernal apart from the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raneth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/8092-dtf-looking-for-ideas-to-put-a-gnostic-spin-to-the-setting?p=9653#post9653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does this impact the setting? How are things different because of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The main complaint I've heard from potential players about DtF is that its quite pessimistic, with either the Fallen being wrong in cuestioning God's Plan(tm) or the Maker being a total douche. My goal is to give the Fallen a higher moral ground and a reason to fight for a higher goal, albeit difficult to attain.<br /> <br /> Rules-wise, I don't thing any changes are necessary, but I think a Gnostic perspective puts the setting under a different light: there <i>is</i> a source of goodness in the world, but the Demiurge cut mankind from it, and the rebels angels fell because they parted the Maker's veil of deception. Perhaps they can set the world right again.<br /> <br /> (as a side note, I'm quite happy with the setting as-is, but I accept not every player is gonna be and that's why I came out with this thought experiment)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/355-romanov","name":"romanov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T10:31:25-08:00","id":12171,"title":"","content":"The Abyss is taken directly from Kabbalah, where it is called Daath.<br /> <br /> There's a Spanish fansplat called Demonio: La Redencion with factions based on their differing beliefs in the nature of God. Some believe God was a tyrant, others think demons were created to tempt and punish sinners, and some try to reclaim the angels they once were. Might be useful for inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1021-raneth","name":"Raneth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}